      "items": [
        {
          "field": "description",
          "fieldtype": "jira",
          "from_string": "*As a* Shopper,\n\n*I want* to see all available colours for a product and be able to switch between them on the page,\n\n*so that* I can explore the full range of colour options before choosing which to buy.\n\nThis story covers the rendering of colour swatches on the PDP and the interaction logic when a shopper selects a different colour. Swatches are driven by the index image — one product image per colour variation that is designated in SFCC BM as the representative swatch image. This story has a hard dependency on the index image attribute being defined and populated in the Product Catalogue epic (Squad A).\n\nColour names are sourced from AP21 via the Product API. The swatch images themselves are not stored in AP21 — they are managed in SFCC.\n\n*In scope:*\n\n* If a product has only one colour, display the colour as a text label (e.g. \"Colour: Bay Blue\") with no swatches rendered\n* If a product has multiple colours, display the index image for each colour variation as a swatch\n* Selecting a colour swatch updates the page content (images, product details) to reflect the selected variation\n* Selecting a colour swatch updates the URL to reflect the selected variation\n* The currently selected colour is visually indicated in the swatch set\n\n*Out of scope:*\n\n* Swatch hover preview — enhancement, not go-live scope\n* Index image attribute definition and population — Product Catalogue epic (Squad A)\n* Image gallery rendering — separate story\n* Size selector — separate story\n\n----\n\n*Acceptance Criteria:*\n\n*Single colour product*\n\nGiven a product has only one colour, when the PDP loads, then the colour is displayed as a text label (e.g. \"Colour: Bay Blue\") and no swatches are rendered.\n\n*Multiple colour products*\n\nGiven a product has multiple colour variations, when the PDP loads, then the index image for each colour variation is displayed as a swatch.\n\nGiven multiple colour swatches are displayed, when the PDP loads, then the currently viewed colour variation's swatch is visually indicated as selected.\n\n*Swatch selection*\n\nGiven a shopper clicks a colour swatch, when the selection is registered, then the page content updates to reflect the selected colour variation.\n\nGiven a shopper clicks a colour swatch, when the selection is registered, then the URL updates to reflect the selected colour variation without a full page reload.\n\nGiven a shopper navigates directly to a colour variation URL, when the page loads, then the correct colour variation is displayed and its swatch is shown as selected.\n\n*Index image not populated*\n\nGiven a colour variation exists but has no index image designated in SFCC, when the PDP loads, then that colour variation's swatch is not rendered and the variation is not surfaced to the shopper (pending confirmation of fallback behaviour — see dependencies).\n\n----\n\n*Dependencies & Open Items:*\n\n* Index image attribute must be defined at variation group level in SFCC BM and populated with sample data before this story can be built or tested — does not currently exist in the Product Catalog Sources sheet and needs to be added to the Product Attributes story (Squad A).\n* Confirm fallback behaviour when a colour variation has no index image populated — should the variation be hidden, shown as a placeholder, or blocked from publishing?\n* Final Figma design in Zimmermann Figma space is pending — swatch design and selected state must be signed off before build begins.",
          "to_string": "*As a* Shopper,\n\n*I want* to see all available colours for a product and be able to switch between them on the page,\n\n*so that* I can explore the full range of colour options before choosing which to buy.\n\n----\n\nImage for reference (final design in Figma is leading):\n\n!image-20260701-114754.png|width=241,alt=\"image-20260701-114754.png\"!\n\nThis story covers the rendering of colour swatches on the PDP and the interaction logic when a shopper selects a different colour. Swatches are driven by the index image — one product image per colour variation that is designated in SFCC BM as the representative swatch image. \n\n----\n\n*Acceptance Criteria:*\n\n\n\n----\n\n*Dependencies & Open Items:*\n\n* Index image attribute must be defined at variation group level in SFCC BM and populated with sample data before this story can be built or tested — does not currently exist in the Product Catalog Sources sheet and needs to be added to the Product Attributes story (Squad A).\n* Confirm fallback behaviour when a colour variation has no index image populated — should the variation be hidden, shown as a placeholder, or blocked from publishing?\n* Final Figma design in Zimmermann Figma space is pending — swatch design and selected state must be signed off before build begins."
        }
      ],
